examiner_comment.text:
"Shifting terms" does not mean changing the terms to different sides at will, but performing the same operation on both sides of the equation.
Take 2x+3=7 as an example:
1) Subtract 3 from both sides at the same time: 2x+3-3=7-3;
2) Simplify to get 2x=4;
3) Divide both sides by 2 at the same time: x=2.
Therefore, the basis for the transfer of terms is the basic property of the equation: if the same number is added (or subtracted) to both sides of the equation at the same time, the equation still holds; if both sides of the equation are multiplied (or divided) by the same number that is not 0, the equation still holds.

